  "commit": "8c2195c8205156f6e3168cc52fa34db334568ea9",
  "labelled_by": "read by hand: every TypeORM call in server/src/repositories/*.repository.ts (NestJS; database.repository.ts left out, as it touches only system catalogs, extensions and tables named at run time) that reads or writes a table. A Repository<E> method (find, findOne, count, exist(s), save, insert, update, upsert, delete, remove, softDelete, softRemove, restore, increment, clear and the like) is labelled on the line of the method name with E's @Entity table, READS for reads and WRITES for writes; save, upsert and softRemove count as WRITES only. An EntityManager method that takes an entity class (clear, upsert, createQueryBuilder(E)) is labelled the same way with that class's table. A query builder is labelled on its createQueryBuilder line with its root table only (the repository's entity, the entity argument, or the table string its from/into names), WRITES when it is an update, delete or insert, READS otherwise, including a builder used only as a subquery or CTE; joined relations are not labelled. A raw query whose SQL is a literal at the call (asset.repository.ts:198, person.repository.ts:52) is labelled with the tables of that SQL. The repositories reach TypeORM through constructor injection (@InjectRepository), through repositories passed by position into the access classes' constructors (access.repository.ts:445-452), and through the repository's own manager and the injected DataSource. The project's own save/create/update wrappers that call those methods are not accesses themselves. Not counted: runtime SET statements, builders over a CTE that name no table, a raw query whose SQL is built elsewhere (search.repository.ts:277), DDL (search.repository.ts:316), a pg_attribute lookup, and Repository.create, which touches no table. The labels are a sample of the repositories folder, so lines outside it are not counted.",
